# {{ project_name }}

A reusable Django app{% if use_shinobi %} with a django-shinobi (Django Ninja) API{% endif %} —
Python {{ python_version }}, Django 5.2 LTS. Install it into any Django project.

## Install

```bash
pip install {{ project_slug }}
```

Add the app to `INSTALLED_APPS`:

```python
INSTALLED_APPS = [
    # ...
    "{{ package_name }}",
]
```
{% if use_shinobi %}

Mount the API router on your project's `NinjaAPI` (or include it in your URLs):

```python
from ninja import NinjaAPI
from {{ package_name }}.api import router as {{ package_name }}_router

api = NinjaAPI()
api.add_router("/{{ package_name }}/", {{ package_name }}_router)
```
{% endif %}

Apply migrations:

```bash
python manage.py migrate
```

## Local development

```bash
uv sync --all-extras --dev
uv run pre-commit install
make test        # pytest against the bundled tests/ settings (sqlite)
make lint        # ruff
make typecheck   # pyright
```

The bundled `example/` project installs this app so you can try it end to end:

```bash
make runserver   # migrates + runs the example project
```

## Packaging

```bash
make build       # build sdist + wheel into dist/
make publish     # build + upload to PyPI (uv publish)
```

